---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ACCURACY NOTE, READ BEFORE EDITING
//
// This policy describes what the site ACTUALLY does today:
//   - sets no cookies of its own
//   - uses one sessionStorage value ("src-tag") for affiliate attribution
//   - has NO analytics installed
//
// The moment you add analytics, ads, embedded video, a newsletter widget or a
// social pixel, this page becomes inaccurate and must be updated. An honest
// short policy is worth far more than a long boilerplate one that claims
// things you do not do.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@thegoodhomelist.online';
const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description={`What ${SITE.name} stores in your browser, what it does not, and what happens when you click through to Amazon.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Cookie Policy' }]} />
    <article class="read prose">
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} does not set any cookies. There are no advertising cookies, no analytics
        cookies, and no tracking pixels on this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is one thing stored in your browser, described below, and there are cookies set by
        Amazon if you click one of our links and leave this site.
      </p>

      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <p>
        This site stores a single value in your browser's <strong>session storage</strong>, under
        the name <code>src-tag</code>. Session storage is separate from cookies. It is never sent
        to a server, it is not shared between sites, and your browser deletes it when you close
        the tab.
      </p>
      <p>The value records which affiliate tracking ID applies to your visit, based on whether
        you arrived from Pinterest or from somewhere else. It lets us tell which channel our
        readers come from. It contains no personal information, no identifier for you, and nothing
        that could be used to recognise you on a later visit or on another site.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you would rather it were not stored, blocking site data for this domain in your browser
        settings prevents it. The site works normally either way.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising or retargeting cookies</li>
        <li>No third-party analytics</li>
        <li>No social media tracking pixels</li>
        <li>No cross-site tracking or profile building</li>
        <li>No selling or sharing of visitor data, because we do not collect any</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies set by Amazon</h2>
      <p>
        This site contains affiliate links to Amazon.com. When you click one, you leave this site
        and arrive on Amazon, and Amazon sets its own cookies at that point. Those cookies record
        that you arrived from here, so that any purchase can be credited to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not control those cookies, cannot read them, and do not receive any information
        about you from them. What we see is an aggregate count of clicks and orders in our
        Amazon Associates dashboard, with no individual visitor attached. Amazon's own privacy
        notice and cookie policy govern what happens once you are on their site.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same applies to any other retailer we may link to in future. Their policies, not ours,
        apply once you leave.
      </p>

      <h2>Embedded content</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not currently embed video players, maps, comment systems or social feeds.
        Those services commonly set their own cookies, so if we add any in future, this page will
        be updated to say so before they go live.
      </p>

      <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
      <p>
        Because we do not track visitors, there is nothing for a Do Not Track signal to disable.
        We honour it by default in the only meaningful way, which is by not collecting the data
        in the first place.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we add analytics or any other service that stores data in your browser, we will update
        this page and change the date at the top before that service goes live.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we will answer.
      </p>

      <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:36px;">
        See also our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> and
        {' '}<a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
